00:02:55.593 --> 00:02:57.380
- That is the interesting thing.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.070
- We talk about people so that

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.020
we can increase our listenership.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.445
- Okay, that's one way to say it.

00:03:03.445 --> 00:03:05.327
- One person at a time,
one victim at a time.

00:03:05.327 --> 00:03:07.130
- But there is this interesting dynamic

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:10.950
of when someone is talked, okay,

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.780
another example of this is
we recently told the story

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.910
of the pooping in the Tupperware.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:17.743
- Oh, oh yeah. (laughs)

00:03:17.743 --> 00:03:21.400
- And then our boys who
were present for that--

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.470
- Right.
- Started a text thread

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.850
and they're like oh, here we go again.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.650
Every time you guys tell this
story, we have to relive it

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.119
and also tell you guys all the
details that you get wrong.

00:03:32.119 --> 00:03:32.952
Including--
- Yeah, and the ones that

00:03:32.952 --> 00:03:34.560
you're getting right that
you used to get wrong

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.580
and the ones that you got right

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:36.650
and now you're getting wrong, it's like--

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.851
- Which is just the psychological concept

00:03:37.851 --> 00:03:40.530
of revisiting a memory and
rewriting it every time,

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.990
it's just the way humans work
but they did clarify one thing

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.410
that I'll clarify now

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.790
and that is that Greg wasn't even there.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.340
- How did he get there?
- I think we've always

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.185
said that Greg was there.

00:03:49.185 --> 00:03:50.930
- I don't even know.
- And somehow,

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.130
Greg wasn't there, so sorry Greg

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.720
for being thrown under
the bus all these years

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.680
and pooping in that Tupperware
that you didn't poop in.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.300
But as is the case with
Ralph when he texted me,

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.100
he was just laughing about
how he'd listen to the thing

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:08.280
and he texted, in quotes,

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.113
Ralph!

00:04:09.113 --> 00:04:11.150
With an exclamation point
because there's the moment

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.820
in the story where I yell out his name.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:15.380
- Yeah.
- And then his son

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:20.380
had taken that moment and cut
it into this just basically--

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.050
- He made a super cut of Ralphs?

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.923
- It was just me saying Ralph!

00:04:24.923 --> 00:04:25.770
Ralph!

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:26.603
Ralph!

00:04:26.603 --> 00:04:27.436
Ralph!

00:04:27.436 --> 00:04:28.269
Ralph!

00:04:28.269 --> 00:04:29.102
Ralph!

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:29.935
Ralph!

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:31.860
- Video or just the audio?
- Video, video.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.190
- Oh yeah, nice.
- And so Ralph

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.330
sent that to me.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.680
So every time we talk about somebody,

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.080
there is, if they listen,
then you have to kinda deal

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.620
with whatever they
think and the super cuts

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.480
of you saying their name.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.570
- Yeah our friendship matrix is crumbling,

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:47.920
I think is another way to put it.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.730
- Which leads me to the
story that I wanna tell you

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.437
because Ralph--

00:04:54.285 --> 00:04:55.880
- Ralph!
- Did also text me,

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.133
he said, what about the waiter story?

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.220
I was like oh crap.
- You didn't tell

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.780
the waiter story.
- I didn't tell anything

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.430
about the waiter, okay so...

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.630
We were in Mammoth, like I said,

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.720
and we had been to Mammoth

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.050
with this exact same family before.

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.923
The year before, Ralph, his wife and kids.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:24.090
And so last year we went to, well,

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.080
I'm trying to think of the
best way to tell this story.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.100
Okay--
- That's something you could

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.770
do before we do a podcast.
- No I like to just--

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:30.800
- That's fine.
- Pull it out of my butt

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.040
as I go.
- That's fine, yeah.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.730
- So there's two parts
to it and I don't know

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.890
which part's better but I
think it's better to start

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.260
with part two and then tell
you how it relates to part one.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:41.410
- You know what, just do
it and then Ralph's son

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:44.770
will edit it in the best way
later and send it to his dad.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:48.110
- So here's what, so we're
eating at this restaurant,

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.360
relatively new restaurant in Mammoth

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.313
and we're all sitting, it's a big group.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.460
There's four of us in our
family, there's five of them,

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.400
that makes nine and so we're
all sitting at this table

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:05.670
and you know the situation
where you're in the middle

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:09.140
of a conversation and a waiter
approaches the table and--

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.650
- They're kinda hovering.
- There's a little bit

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:14.140
of a power play that happens
and some waiters are better

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.870
at managing the situation than others

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.740
and there's also people, interestingly,

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.820
I think this might even
play into our conversations

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:24.240
of who's, what we're like in real life,

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.020
as an example, if you're in
the middle of saying something

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.021
in real life and a waiter comes up,

00:06:31.021 --> 00:06:34.330
chances that you stop for
the waiter are pretty small.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.740
If I'm telling something
and a waiter comes up,

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.310
chances are pretty high
that I'm going to stop.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.560
That's just, you may
think that's the opposite

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.800
of the way it would be but in real life,

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.450
that's actually, it might
be 'cause you don't notice

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:47.500
but you're also one to be like,

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:48.610
I'm gonna get this thought out

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:52.400
and then there'll be a
break and this guy can say,

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:55.638
but so, somebody else was talking

00:06:55.638 --> 00:06:59.170
and didn't see this waiter standing there.

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:01.830
And he stood there and
he just started going...

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.810
Like making a mouth noise.
- Chewing something?

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:09.530
- Was like, this is his warning system.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.973
It was awkward, and eventually,

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:17.130
the conversation came to a
close and he stood there,

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:19.860
made one last mouth smacking noise

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.323
and then paused.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:26.133
It's weird and
uncomfortable, and then said,

00:07:27.317 --> 00:07:29.960
"Hello folks, how are you today?"

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:34.960
And then proceeded to do
the normal waiter things

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:38.210
but in a way that his energy made me feel

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:40.110
and everyone else feel uncomfortable.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.690
It was just like--
- It was an animosity?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.570
- No no, it was not an animosity at all,

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.450
it was just a weirdness.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:49.810
It was a social weirdness
that just made us feel strange

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:50.993
and like--
- Well.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:54.960
- Just pausing at certain
times and then staying

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:57.070
in one place and then
not leaving early enough

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:58.260
after you're like, you
finished a sentence.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.380
It was like everything
was a little bit off time

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:03.380
in a way that just makes you
feel uncomfortable and uneasy.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.420
So he has this interaction
with us and then he leaves

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.670
and everybody's kinda
like that was kinda weird,

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:10.103
and then I was like hold on a second.

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:15.140
I'm gonna change his name
because I legitimately

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.330
don't want this guy to
listen to this podcast.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.330
- Call him Justin.

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.210
- Justin.
- What if his name was Justin

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.153
and I suggested it and you're like--

00:08:21.153 --> 00:08:23.343
- It wasn't.
- Let's not call him Justin.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:29.470
- I was like, our waiter's name is Justin.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:32.360
- What, okay.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.630
You just said what the waiter's name,

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.304
you knew the waiter's real
name which isn't Justin

00:08:36.304 --> 00:08:38.770
and you said it.
- And I said last year,

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:43.370
at a different restaurant, we
had this exact same experience

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.760
and exact same conversation--

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.950
- Did they remember it?
- And everybody started being

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:50.380
like oh you're right,
that is the same guy,

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.850
the same haircut and the
mustache and it's the same guy.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:55.930
It's Justin.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.640
And he proceeds to do exactly
the same thing that he did

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.230
the first time which we
got such a kick out of it

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.710
the first time around, like
this guy was so awkward

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:08.057
and the way he would pause
and the way he would stay

00:09:08.057 --> 00:09:09.563
at your table and then,

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.630
like imagine just you're
taking somebody's order

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:17.193
and then as you get done, you're like,

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.400
is there anything else you need?

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.970
And you're like nope and he's just like--

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:23.410
- It's like a robot downloading--

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.150
- He waits four seconds--
- His next line.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:27.200
- Makes you feel weird
like what is going on?

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.030
And then he did it again, his
technique, new restaurant,

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:33.330
same technique, and--

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:35.080
- You think he got fired
from the other place

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.660
for his pauses and whatnot?

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.760
- No because first of all, I was like,

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.723
he came back and I was
like, Justin, right?

00:09:43.669 --> 00:09:45.169
He was like yeah, I was like--

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:50.750
- I remember you, your weird
waitering from last year.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:52.787
- I said, "You were
our waiter last year at

00:09:52.787 --> 00:09:55.220
"blah blah blah blah
restaurant in Mammoth,"

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:58.346
and he said, "Oh yeah, I
don't miss that place."

00:09:58.346 --> 00:09:59.179
(laughs)
- Oh.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.530
- And okay, I don't know what happened.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:07.090
I'm not gonna ask any
questions but it was just,

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:11.700
it was a, it was just one of those moments

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.680
that this guy left this--
- He didn't remember anything.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.440
- Indelible mark on us
and then he did it again

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:20.817
and we realized deja vu
way, it was happening

00:10:20.817 --> 00:10:22.430
at the same time and we're like no,

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.800
it's just the same guy happening
at a different restaurant.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.790
This is what he does.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:28.290
- And the moral of the story,

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:29.460
no there doesn't have to be a moral

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.803
but here's the freaky thing.

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:36.210
It reminds me of a story I
didn't tell you but from Cabo

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:37.167
which is very short and it's not much--

00:10:37.167 --> 00:10:39.310
- You had a weird waiter?

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:41.030
- Well you know, as I explained,

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.150
I went back to the same, we
went back to the same resort

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:44.940
that we had gone to
like a couple of years.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.580
Actually it may have
been three years early

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.280
the more I thought about it, okay?

00:10:49.995 --> 00:10:52.590
And there's a restaurant at The Cape

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:57.600
and the first night we
were there, both times,

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.890
we've made a reservation
there 'cause it's really nice,

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:01.110
it's a really good restaurant.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:04.607
And we went there and we
sat, they were gonna seat us

00:11:04.607 --> 00:11:06.640
and I was like can you seat us outside?

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:07.750
'Cause I was thinking it was great,

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.200
it's what we did last time.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:13.010
We go, we sit outside
and then all of a sudden,

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:14.853
the waiter comes up
and he's like asking us

00:11:14.853 --> 00:11:16.553
have we been here, we're like yes.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.770
We get our waters.

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.763
He goes away and I'm like, Christy.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:27.670
That is the same waiter
from three years ago.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.100
Same guy.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.570
And then he comes back up and we're like,

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:33.800
we're looking at him and
