01:01:08.260 --> 01:01:10.260
and didn't let you finish a story or,

01:01:10.260 --> 01:01:11.140
we would just...

01:01:13.940 --> 01:01:16.540
We had so much to learn but the thing

01:01:16.540 --> 01:01:19.123
that I'm learning now
is I'm actually seeing,

01:01:21.440 --> 01:01:23.490
and maybe this plays into
people feeling sorry for me

01:01:23.490 --> 01:01:25.180
'cause I don't want people
to feel sorry for me

01:01:25.180 --> 01:01:27.570
and say oh, Link's the butt of the joke

01:01:27.570 --> 01:01:29.910
or everybody thinks he's stupid,

01:01:29.910 --> 01:01:33.118
or maybe he is stupid
and I feel sorry for him.

01:01:33.118 --> 01:01:37.950
I don't want any of that
because I think I've actually...

01:01:40.360 --> 01:01:42.523
The game show thing is a good example.

01:01:43.610 --> 01:01:47.110
But in pretty much every episode,

01:01:47.110 --> 01:01:49.753
I'm finding out how,

01:01:50.940 --> 01:01:55.330
more of my true instincts
can be harnessed for comedy,

01:01:55.330 --> 01:01:57.423
and so the more honest I am,

01:01:59.065 --> 01:02:00.360
and I think I've been
thinking about it more

01:02:00.360 --> 01:02:02.210
since we talked about the Instagram thing.

01:02:02.210 --> 01:02:04.870
When you talked about dude,
you just do what you wanna do

01:02:04.870 --> 01:02:09.870
on Instagram, like you
planning out something is,

01:02:09.881 --> 01:02:13.363
you're short-circuiting
your own comedic process.

01:02:14.490 --> 01:02:16.263
So dance like nobody's watching.

01:02:18.110 --> 01:02:22.100
Anyway, I actually think
that, in the exercise

01:02:22.100 --> 01:02:24.190
of doing that within the context of GMM

01:02:24.190 --> 01:02:25.800
and understanding what I'm trying to do

01:02:25.800 --> 01:02:27.150
that I'm just trying to...

01:02:30.840 --> 01:02:33.190
Thinking of it as
suspending my intelligence

01:02:33.190 --> 01:02:36.120
and knowing that like
okay, I'm not an idiot.

01:02:36.120 --> 01:02:40.180
I'm actually smart for
being able to harness

01:02:40.180 --> 01:02:42.700
just raw instinct in this way.

01:02:42.700 --> 01:02:44.940
I actually feel better
about it. (chuckles)

01:02:44.940 --> 01:02:47.220
But then a step further, I actually

01:02:48.690 --> 01:02:53.690
feel like that the show me

01:02:55.260 --> 01:02:58.140
is kind of a gateway to me
introducing some of that

01:02:58.140 --> 01:03:00.589
back into my real life.

01:03:00.589 --> 01:03:04.830
I've taken as an exercise
to just say, you know what,

01:03:04.830 --> 01:03:06.300
I'm going to...

01:03:10.386 --> 01:03:11.890
I'm gonna go on instinct.

01:03:11.890 --> 01:03:13.520
I'm gonna be experiencing this moment.

01:03:13.520 --> 01:03:15.020
I'm not gonna overthink it.

01:03:15.020 --> 01:03:20.020
I'm not going to be so serious
or give into my anxiety

01:03:20.490 --> 01:03:25.490
or whatever maybe is what is instinctively

01:03:25.780 --> 01:03:29.480
in my normal life, the first concern

01:03:29.480 --> 01:03:32.710
that would enter my mind but
then saying, you know what,

01:03:32.710 --> 01:03:35.645
this is what it's like to have fun.

01:03:35.645 --> 01:03:39.580
And I think the exercise of
doing the show builds the muscle

01:03:39.580 --> 01:03:44.580
of being able to let loose
a little bit and then...

01:03:45.960 --> 01:03:50.610
So in the way that I play
with the kids or hang out

01:03:50.610 --> 01:03:52.480
with Christy or when I get home from work

01:03:52.480 --> 01:03:55.240
and we're all hanging out in
the kitchen and it's like,

01:03:55.240 --> 01:03:56.770
oh we're playing music, and you know what,

01:03:56.770 --> 01:04:00.860
I'm just gonna, you
know what, let's dance.

01:04:00.860 --> 01:04:04.047
We funneled so much of that energy

01:04:04.047 --> 01:04:08.821
to your point of we're
boring into our work

01:04:08.821 --> 01:04:12.143
that from a practical standpoint,

01:04:14.490 --> 01:04:17.120
I felt like it's all
been drained out of me.

01:04:17.120 --> 01:04:20.170
So I don't know maybe I'm
getting a little too--

01:04:20.170 --> 01:04:22.330
- Well.
- I'm just trying to,

01:04:22.330 --> 01:04:24.920
I'm actually trying to harness
that in my every day life

01:04:24.920 --> 01:04:27.143
to just become generally stupid.

01:04:27.143 --> 01:04:29.170
- Well I think--
- But you know what I mean.

01:04:29.170 --> 01:04:32.050
- I think what I was saying was that

01:04:32.050 --> 01:04:35.290
people might expect that if
I were to just watch Rhett

01:04:35.290 --> 01:04:38.100
and Link having a
conversation with each other,

01:04:38.100 --> 01:04:40.758
then it would be--
- Hilarious.

01:04:40.758 --> 01:04:42.685
- It would be hilarious
and as entertaining

01:04:42.685 --> 01:04:46.490
as an Ear Biscuit.

01:04:46.490 --> 01:04:47.323
- Right.

01:04:47.323 --> 01:04:50.250
- When in reality, it would
probably be as entertaining

01:04:50.250 --> 01:04:53.240
as the last half hour of this Ear Biscuit,

01:04:53.240 --> 01:04:55.234
you know what I'm saying, which,

01:04:55.234 --> 01:04:57.560
you might be like oh
this is the good stuff.

01:04:57.560 --> 01:04:58.760
They got very real.

01:04:58.760 --> 01:05:00.060
But you probably didn't last a whole lot

01:05:00.060 --> 01:05:01.323
in the past 30 minutes.

01:05:02.330 --> 01:05:05.853
I'm just saying that that's
kinda how we talk to each other.

01:05:07.050 --> 01:05:08.050
For me...

01:05:12.731 --> 01:05:14.950
I feel like for me it's not a question

01:05:14.950 --> 01:05:19.621
of I don't have enough personality
left over for my family.

01:05:19.621 --> 01:05:22.720
A lot of times it's
just an energy question

01:05:22.720 --> 01:05:25.680
or a time question because
I gotta work on this thing.

01:05:25.680 --> 01:05:27.600
Even though I'm at home
I gotta finish this thing

01:05:27.600 --> 01:05:29.955
and that's a problem, but that's not,

01:05:29.955 --> 01:05:31.660
that's a different problem,

01:05:31.660 --> 01:05:33.140
that's like a time management problem.

01:05:33.140 --> 01:05:35.040
- I wasn't directing any of it at you.

01:05:37.254 --> 01:05:40.440
I think that the moments
where we just embrace

01:05:40.440 --> 01:05:42.750
the sheer joy of what happens on the show

01:05:42.750 --> 01:05:47.750
and we heighten it I think
is a skill that was like,

01:05:47.800 --> 01:05:52.722
okay, how can this cycle back ironically

01:05:52.722 --> 01:05:57.722
and the life could imitate art

01:05:59.220 --> 01:06:00.659
and I could benefit from it.

01:06:00.659 --> 01:06:02.680
So it was an interesting thought exercise.

01:06:02.680 --> 01:06:04.360
- Well along the same lines,

01:06:04.360 --> 01:06:05.990
I don't even know if you
were in this conversation

01:06:05.990 --> 01:06:08.720
with some of our close friends,
we were talking about...

01:06:13.470 --> 01:06:18.470
I'm trying to figure out some things

01:06:18.550 --> 01:06:20.220
in therapy like we've been talking about,

01:06:20.220 --> 01:06:22.200
like being able to understand
what my emotions are

01:06:22.200 --> 01:06:24.163
and deal with feelings
and that kinda thing.

01:06:25.530 --> 01:06:30.280
But I think part of that is like we have,

01:06:30.280 --> 01:06:31.490
we've got a friend group

01:06:31.490 --> 01:06:35.140
and there's a very high
emotional intelligence

01:06:35.140 --> 01:06:36.373
in our friend group.

01:06:37.670 --> 01:06:40.550
Like significantly higher
than I have sort of

01:06:41.750 --> 01:06:44.810
been close to for the majority of my life.

01:06:44.810 --> 01:06:45.860
- Mm-hmm.

01:06:45.860 --> 01:06:46.760
- Not judging you.

01:06:48.500 --> 01:06:49.620
Just saying just in terms

01:06:49.620 --> 01:06:51.623
of like greater friendships or whatever.

01:06:53.170 --> 01:06:57.900
And I mean they're all legitimately
just intelligent people

01:06:57.900 --> 01:07:00.300
but they're also emotionally intelligent

01:07:00.300 --> 01:07:02.681
and what I mean by that
is somebody's going

01:07:02.681 --> 01:07:05.220
through something or
somebody shares something

01:07:05.220 --> 01:07:09.290
and they just have just a level of insight

01:07:09.290 --> 01:07:14.290
and perspective that I'm
kind of used to being,

01:07:15.223 --> 01:07:17.850
I like kinda being the
guy who knows things

01:07:17.850 --> 01:07:19.380
in the room, right, you know that

01:07:19.380 --> 01:07:20.437
and it annoys you.

01:07:21.306 --> 01:07:23.320
And I understand that.

01:07:23.320 --> 01:07:26.840
But like, then a lot of places,

01:07:26.840 --> 01:07:29.000
I am the guy who knows
things in the room, right?

01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:31.080
I'm not an expert on
anything but I know a lot

01:07:31.080 --> 01:07:35.470
about a lot of things and
so I tend to feel like

01:07:35.470 --> 01:07:37.360
I've got something to contribute

01:07:37.360 --> 01:07:39.440
but a lot of times with the group

01:07:39.440 --> 01:07:41.160
that we've gotten really close with,

01:07:41.160 --> 01:07:42.550
they're so emotionally intelligent

01:07:42.550 --> 01:07:44.903
that I start to kinda feel like an idiot.

01:07:46.200 --> 01:07:49.730
And I'm like, I don't know
how to comfort this person.

01:07:49.730 --> 01:07:52.310
I don't know what to say in this situation

01:07:52.310 --> 01:07:54.910
because that's not how my brain works.

01:07:54.910 --> 01:07:56.750
I haven't figured that out yet

01:07:56.750 --> 01:07:58.993
and so I'm just gonna kinda be quiet.

01:08:01.610 --> 01:08:05.550
And I've also done a
second level of analysis.

01:08:05.550 --> 01:08:07.924
Again, we've hinted at the Enneagram

01:08:07.924 --> 01:08:11.760
and we will do an episode
about it at some point.

01:08:11.760 --> 01:08:14.610
But again it's the personality evaluation

01:08:14.610 --> 01:08:16.160
where there's nine
different personality types.

01:08:16.160 --> 01:08:19.660
I'm a three on the Enneagram
which means I'm a performer,

01:08:19.660 --> 01:08:24.230
an achiever and one of the
things that the threes do is

01:08:24.230 --> 01:08:27.580
that if they are not good at something,

01:08:27.580 --> 01:08:28.933
they don't play the game.

01:08:30.340 --> 01:08:35.070
And so, engaging on an emotional level

01:08:35.070 --> 01:08:36.480
with somebody is something I'm not good at

01:08:36.480 --> 01:08:38.050
so I just don't do it.

01:08:38.050 --> 01:08:40.750
Because I do the things that I can win at

01:08:40.750 --> 01:08:43.120
and that is a, and I
didn't really understand

01:08:43.120 --> 01:08:45.310
that's how my personality worked

01:08:45.310 --> 01:08:47.530
until I started reading more in depth

01:08:47.530 --> 01:08:49.170
about the way threes are and it's like,

01:08:49.170 --> 01:08:51.510
if they don't have a good
chance of winning the game,

01:08:51.510 --> 01:08:53.170
they do not participate.

01:08:53.170 --> 01:08:55.100
And they can actually
be incredibly successful

01:08:55.100 --> 01:08:56.800
because they are good at a lot of things

01:08:56.800 --> 01:08:59.260
and they also only do the
things they're good at

01:08:59.260 --> 01:09:01.410
so you see them and you're
like, man they're good

01:09:01.410 --> 01:09:02.548
at all the things that they do

01:09:02.548 --> 01:09:04.527
until you put them in an
environment where they have

01:09:04.527 --> 01:09:07.870
to behave differently so
the way this translates

01:09:07.870 --> 01:09:09.757
to the difference between me on the show

01:09:09.757 --> 01:09:14.005
and me in real life is that
when I get into those situations

01:09:14.005 --> 01:09:18.551
where I feel like it's a
more intimate atmosphere,

01:09:18.551 --> 01:09:21.581
I become the quiet one.

01:09:21.581 --> 01:09:24.073
Where on the show, there's no opportunity

01:09:24.073 --> 01:09:25.430
to be the quiet one.

01:09:25.430 --> 01:09:26.720
Neither one of us is the quiet one.

01:09:26.720 --> 01:09:29.580
We both could talk 100 miles an hour.

01:09:29.580 --> 01:09:31.670
We talk over each other
constantly because we both want

01:09:31.670 --> 01:09:33.500
to be the ones to get the last word in.

01:09:33.500 --> 01:09:35.750
I think we both suffer
from that and that's one

01:09:35.750 --> 01:09:37.650
of the things that
contributes to why we do

01:09:37.650 --> 01:09:39.100
what we do and we do it well.

01:09:40.713 --> 01:09:44.480
And so the thing I told our friends

01:09:44.480 --> 01:09:48.160
when I was talking is I
actually think that my true self

01:09:48.160 --> 01:09:51.560
is more represented in
the context of what I do

01:09:51.560 --> 01:09:55.080
as an entertainer than it is
when I'm just in real life.

01:09:55.080 --> 01:10:00.080
When I am my more
happy-go-lucky, in the moment,

01:10:00.129 --> 01:10:03.700
reacting, laughing, trying
to make people laugh,

01:10:03.700 --> 01:10:06.420
thing that I do on the show,

01:10:06.420 --> 01:10:09.300
and even in the context of
this, I'm still on a little bit.

01:10:09.300 --> 01:10:10.863
- Yeah.
- My on

01:10:10.863 --> 01:10:13.070
is actually--

01:10:13.070 --> 01:10:14.390
- Letting something out.

01:10:14.390 --> 01:10:16.640
- A truer connection with who I am.

01:10:16.640 --> 01:10:18.510
It isn't putting something on.

01:10:18.510 --> 01:10:23.510
In fact, the mask and
the facade is the quiet,

01:10:25.826 --> 01:10:28.840
reserved Rhett who is afraid to enter

01:10:28.840 --> 01:10:31.370
into a certain situation
for fear of not being able

01:10:31.370 --> 01:10:34.210
to win that situation because
I frame it in the wrong way.

01:10:34.210 --> 01:10:35.850
- That's exactly what I'm talking about.

01:10:35.850 --> 01:10:39.650
I think yeah, within
the context of the show,

01:10:39.650 --> 01:10:44.650
you can experience legitimate
emotion within a certain,

01:10:44.700 --> 01:10:49.186
a subset of emotions, right,
that are like elation,

01:10:49.186 --> 01:10:50.410
as an example.

01:10:50.410 --> 01:10:51.520
- Well I think it goes to--
- It's a discovery.

01:10:51.520 --> 01:10:53.733
- Show you that--
- Surprise.

01:10:53.733 --> 01:10:55.920
- Unbelievably--
- Pain.

01:10:55.920 --> 01:10:57.950
- And thankfully.
- Happiness.

01:10:57.950 --> 01:11:01.535
- We've created an environment on the show

01:11:01.535 --> 01:11:04.900
where we can be so
comfortable, 'cause again,

01:11:04.900 --> 01:11:06.870
this is the thing that we
didn't get when we did,

01:11:06.870 --> 01:11:10.270
like if you go back and watch
the old Online Nation clips,

01:11:10.270 --> 01:11:12.120
you look at that and you're
like, we were not comfortable.

01:11:12.120 --> 01:11:12.953
- Oh no.
- Right?

01:11:12.953 --> 01:11:16.100
It was the peak of the evidence
that there is out there

01:11:16.100 --> 01:11:18.970
of us not being comfortable
in a entertainment setting.

01:11:18.970 --> 01:11:19.960
- Yeah.

01:11:19.960 --> 01:11:23.880
- But this show and GMM also
represent these environments

01:11:23.880 --> 01:11:27.950
that we've created and we've been able

01:11:27.950 --> 01:11:31.480
to completely shape the
environment so that we can just

01:11:31.480 --> 01:11:33.230
be our true selves.

01:11:33.230 --> 01:11:36.050
So it is ironic that it
seems like oh you're on

01:11:36.050 --> 01:11:39.510
and you're acting, but my
theory and I hear you saying

01:11:39.510 --> 01:11:40.800
the same thing is that well, actually,

01:11:40.800 --> 01:11:43.260
that's who I am and when I go out

01:11:43.260 --> 01:11:46.560
and I navigate the real
world, I turn that,

01:11:46.560 --> 01:11:49.863
it isn't that I turn it
on when I'm on the show,

01:11:49.863 --> 01:11:52.180
it's that I turn it off
when I'm in real life.

01:11:52.180 --> 01:11:54.160
- Yeah I think that we've...

01:11:57.826 --> 01:12:00.410
I think my question to the listener

01:12:00.410 --> 01:12:05.350
or to the Mythical Beasts
watching GMM who complains

01:12:05.350 --> 01:12:08.070
about things that maybe
they're missing the comedy

01:12:08.070 --> 01:12:11.200
or they're misinterpreting
a comedic choice

01:12:11.200 --> 01:12:14.490
as an honest moment and
then being disappointed

01:12:14.490 --> 01:12:15.960
and then being critical of it,

01:12:15.960 --> 01:12:20.960
I'm asking them to
expand the way they view

01:12:21.345 --> 01:12:23.290
our performance in the show,

01:12:23.290 --> 01:12:27.210
to not shift but to include those things.

01:12:27.210 --> 01:12:29.160
I think that's what I'm asking of them.

01:12:30.063 --> 01:12:33.360
And I know that it
frustrates you a little more

01:12:33.360 --> 01:12:35.460
than it does to me because it kinda,

01:12:35.460 --> 01:12:37.040
as we've discussed, it goes to you.

01:12:37.040 --> 01:12:42.040
But I think for you maybe
there's an opportunity

01:12:42.676 --> 01:12:46.380
to see, I think you just
described the beauty

01:12:46.380 --> 01:12:47.513
of what the show,

01:12:48.930 --> 01:12:52.610
the opportunity it gives you as a person

01:12:52.610 --> 01:12:56.170
and me as a person to
experience things that can then

01:12:56.170 --> 01:12:58.910
inspire who we are in our normal lives.

01:12:58.910 --> 01:13:02.055
And those are the things
that people, they latch,

01:13:02.055 --> 01:13:06.850
those true moments, if they
latch onto them so hard

01:13:06.850 --> 01:13:09.510
and make them so precious
that they can't take

01:13:09.510 --> 01:13:12.470
the other comedic bits, it's like,

01:13:12.470 --> 01:13:14.270
you can't fault 'em for it.

01:13:14.270 --> 01:13:17.280
Because it's also a very,
it's kind of the heart

01:13:17.280 --> 01:13:19.070
and soul of our show because like--

01:13:19.070 --> 01:13:21.947
- We've created an environment
where we're authentic

01:13:21.947 --> 01:13:24.860
and so then to get upset with them

01:13:24.860 --> 01:13:29.130
for being, for doing a
character or doing a bit

01:13:29.130 --> 01:13:32.300
and having a problem with it, it's yeah.

01:13:32.300 --> 01:13:33.133
- It's kind of a meeting in the middle.

01:13:33.133 --> 01:13:34.900
- I just wanna have my
cake and eat it too.

01:13:34.900 --> 01:13:38.244
- Yeah taking that criticism as an,

01:13:38.244 --> 01:13:40.870
you can invert it as a
compliment that like,

01:13:40.870 --> 01:13:42.700
the thing that attracts them
to the show is the heart

01:13:42.700 --> 01:13:46.910
and soul of the show and it's
our true selves coming through

01:13:46.910 --> 01:13:50.280
and they can't even take
it when we make a choice

01:13:50.280 --> 01:13:51.397
that deviates from it so--

01:13:51.397 --> 01:13:53.566
- I think--
- Maybe that'll just help,

01:13:53.566 --> 01:13:55.210
just help you process it.

01:13:55.210 --> 01:13:58.210
- Well and also we talked about
this a little bit is I think

01:13:58.210 --> 01:14:03.210
that unfortunately the
people who have an issue

01:14:03.689 --> 01:14:07.180
with these types of things
are also for whatever reason,

01:14:07.180 --> 01:14:09.060
the personality profile
is they're more likely

01:14:09.060 --> 01:14:11.720
to engage online, and so the people

01:14:11.720 --> 01:14:14.627
who might actually appreciate--

01:14:14.627 --> 01:14:18.590
- And I think ultimately
we're different people

01:14:18.590 --> 01:14:22.570
and I think better people
because of fielding that.

01:14:22.570 --> 01:14:24.900
As painful or frustrating
as it may be sometimes too,

01:14:24.900 --> 01:14:26.300
so I'll even go that for.

01:14:26.300 --> 01:14:27.370
You need to be thankful for it.

01:14:27.370 --> 01:14:30.060
- I don't disagree with
that I'm just saying that

01:14:30.060 --> 01:14:33.200
one of the things that
makes it difficult is that

01:14:33.200 --> 01:14:35.852
I know that there are people
out there who appreciate

01:14:35.852 --> 01:14:39.240
but you're likely to get
a comment about something

01:14:39.240 --> 01:14:41.470
that they don't like than they do like.

01:14:41.470 --> 01:14:46.470
We get so many, when we meet
fans in meet and greet lines

01:14:47.890 --> 01:14:52.270
at shows, I'm always surprised

01:14:52.270 --> 01:14:54.360
with how many people have
Cotton Candy Randy t-shirts on

01:14:54.360 --> 01:14:56.830
and say I love Cotton Candy Randy.

01:14:56.830 --> 01:14:59.150
And I'm like well why
don't you say something

01:14:59.150 --> 01:15:01.010
on the internet about it? (laughs)

01:15:01.010 --> 01:15:02.030
You know what I'm saying?

01:15:02.030 --> 01:15:04.820
It's like, and so--

01:15:04.820 --> 01:15:06.370
- Well do you want a
comment or do you want them

01:15:06.370 --> 01:15:07.610
to buy a shirt?

01:15:07.610 --> 01:15:09.250
- Well how about both?

01:15:09.250 --> 01:15:10.984
No but you're right and again,

